# Copy to .env for local runs (Next.js and the admin both read it; never commit real values). All are optional locally.
# On Vercel, set these in Project Settings -> Environment Variables. docs/vercel.md is the full reference (purpose,
# required or optional, which environments, build time or runtime); test/next/env.test.ts keeps both files complete.

# ---- Password gate ----
# Master password: opens every site, every site's own domain, the landing page (/ by default; /all when a root site is configured) and the component gallery (/_gallery).
# Required on every Vercel deployment (NODE_ENV=production, previews included) unless PREVIEW_PUBLIC=true:
# without it the proxy answers 503 instead of serving.
PREVIEW_PASSWORD=
# Optional per-site passwords, PREVIEW_PASSWORD_<SLUG> (open only that site, on the hub and on its own domain, plus
# shared assets), e.g. PREVIEW_PASSWORD_SPURS=. Hyphens in a slug become underscores: man-utd -> PREVIEW_PASSWORD_MAN_UTD
# true turns the password gate off in production. Pages stay noindex, so this is not a launch switch
# (that is site.json -> indexable; see docs/content-model.md).
PREVIEW_PUBLIC=

# ---- Origins and hosts (read at build time: redeploy after changing) ----
# The hub's origin in canonical, Open Graph, sitemap and structured-data URLs, e.g. https://appearances.getapeptalk.com
# If unset: https://$VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL (never a partner domain), else https://appearances.getapeptalk.com.
# A value that isn't an http(s) origin is ignored (logged at build). Sites with a live domain use that domain instead.
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=
# The hub's host: the only host where a live site's folder answers 301 to its own domain (docs/domains.md).
# Default: PUBLIC_ORIGIN's host, else appearances.getapeptalk.com.
# HUB_HOST=appearances.getapeptalk.com
# off switches search indexing off everywhere, whatever site.json says (kill switch; redeploy to apply).
# Vercel preview deployments (VERCEL_ENV=preview) never index anyway.
# SEARCH_INDEXING=off

# ---- Enquiry form (POST /api/enquiry; docs/vercel.md -> Enquiry webhook) ----
# When set (https; http only for localhost), enquiries are forwarded there as JSON. Unset: they are checked and
# discarded, nothing is sent or stored, and the form shows the concept confirmation. Read at build time by the form
# and at request time by the endpoint, so redeploy after changing it.
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/appearances
# Sent as the X-Enquiry-Secret header with every forwarded enquiry.
# ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ---- Tracking (off by default; docs/architecture.md -> Tracking and consent) ----
# Global Google Tag Manager container for sites without site.json -> tracking. Must look like GTM-XXXXXXX.
# TRACKING_GTM_ID=

# ---- Content providers (lib/content/, docs/content-contract.md) ----
# CONTENT_PROVIDER=json   # json | cms (the CMS provider is a stub until implemented)
# PEOPLE_PROVIDER=json    # json | airtable (people for the sites listed in the Airtable config; docs/airtable-cms.md)

# Airtable people sync (only with PEOPLE_PROVIDER=airtable). Never commit the token.
# Personal access token: scope data.records:read, access to the one base only.
# AIRTABLE_TOKEN=
# The sync config as inline JSON (preferred on Vercel), or a path to it (default config/airtable.json).
# See config/airtable.example.json.
# AIRTABLE_CONFIG=
# AIRTABLE_CONFIG_FILE=config/airtable.json

# Extra image hosts (comma-separated https origins, e.g. your R2 bucket) allowed by next/image and the CSP, for
# images that may appear after a deploy. Hosts already in the content are allowed automatically. Read at build time.
# IMAGE_HOSTS_EXTRA=https://media.example.com

# ---- Revalidation webhook (POST /api/revalidate; docs/content-contract.md -> Revalidation) ----
# Shared secret for CMS and Airtable webhooks, sent as the x-revalidate-secret header. Answers on every host (the hub,
# previews, each site's domain), outside the password gate. Unset: the endpoint answers 503.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# ---- Set by Vercel or Next.js (don't set them) ----
# VERCEL_ENV (previews never index), VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (shown by /health), VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL (origin
# fallback; enable "Enable access to System Environment Variables"), VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_ID (scopes the content
# cache to the deployment), NODE_ENV (production on every deployment).

# ---- Internal (set by the build or the tests; never set them on Vercel) ----
# APPEARANCES_MANIFEST (inlined by next.config.ts), NEXT_DIST_DIR (build directory; tests use .next-test),
# APPEARANCES_SITES_DIR (content directory; tests point it at fixture content)
# Set by next.config.ts during a build:
# APPEARANCES_CACHE_SCOPE      the content cache scope (VERCEL_DEPLOYMENT_ID, else a random id per build)
# APPEARANCES_BUILD_SNAPSHOT   directory where the build shares remote people with its workers (OS temp dir)

# ---- Contract tests only (npm run contract; docs/content-contract.md) ----
# CONTRACT_FAILING_ENV={"CMS_API_URL":"http://127.0.0.1:9"}   env overrides that break the source (typed-error check)
# CONTRACT_FETCH_IMAGES=1                                       also fetch every image URL once

# ---- Local tools ----
# Chrome/Chromium binary for npm run og-cards, visual, perf and perf:budget, if it is not found automatically.
# CHROME_PATH=

# Local admin (npm run admin; see docs/admin.md). Binds to 127.0.0.1:3095 by default.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# ADMIN_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ADMIN_PORT=3095
# Optional GitHub storage: saves become commits on a content/admin-… branch with a PR (set both to enable).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_REPO=owner/name
# GITHUB_BASE=main
